WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:01.970
Ga Ga Gah!

00:00:04.870 --> 00:00:06.380
Hey, how'd you know that old ratty cop

00:00:06.410 --> 00:00:08.120
out there? Or whatever?

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:11.730
So we're back to this now.

00:00:12.330 --> 00:00:14.670
Fine. I can play the quiet game too.

00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:21.430
Why won't you talk?

00:00:23.650 --> 00:00:25.400
Why won't you talk? Why won't you talk?

00:00:25.420 --> 00:00:25.990
Why won't you talk?

00:00:26.080 --> 00:00:27.110
Why do you talk so much.

00:00:27.130 --> 00:00:28.420
This mouth has gotten me out of a lot of

00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:29.690
sticky situations.

00:00:29.850 --> 00:00:31.450
Ew. Not like that?

00:00:31.840 --> 00:00:33.100
I mean, that happened to.

00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:37.590
Out here. Silence can get you killed.

00:00:37.620 --> 00:00:38.940
Silence kept me alive.

00:00:38.940 --> 00:00:39.450
Oh, yeah?

00:00:39.480 --> 00:00:40.980
So why would you tell that cop to eat

00:00:40.980 --> 00:00:41.850
your ass?

00:00:50.890 --> 00:00:53.110
Well, Hello. It's a mystery.

00:00:53.140 --> 00:00:55.450
How our paths just keep crossing.

00:00:57.190 --> 00:00:58.750
My men say that you have.

00:00:59.700 --> 00:01:02.030
You have a darling voice.

00:01:03.160 --> 00:01:04.660
I'm excited to hear what comes out of

00:01:04.660 --> 00:01:04.930
it.

00:01:05.760 --> 00:01:08.010
You need better f***ing friends, dude.

00:01:13.650 --> 00:01:14.850
Go ahead. Drink up.

00:01:27.090 --> 00:01:30.060
Oh, where we were sitting there once

00:01:30.060 --> 00:01:32.220
flowed a powerful river.

00:01:32.250 --> 00:01:34.200
Then they built this architectural

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:36.240
marvel. My father used to bring me here

00:01:36.240 --> 00:01:37.800
for the tour when I was a child.

00:01:38.620 --> 00:01:41.200
The tour? It's a bit dry.

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:43.170
Hah!

00:01:43.170 --> 00:01:44.820
It's a little dam humor for you.

00:01:45.240 --> 00:01:47.550
But now the roads have all become wild

00:01:47.550 --> 00:01:49.320
rivers. So I'm building my own

00:01:49.320 --> 00:01:51.090
blockade. A dam, if you will.

00:01:51.120 --> 00:01:53.400
It runs from southern Arizona all the

00:01:53.400 --> 00:01:55.410
way to the Canadian wastes.

00:01:56.360 --> 00:01:58.340
But the only way through.

00:02:00.210 --> 00:02:03.560
Is here. Wow.

00:02:03.580 --> 00:02:05.020
Cool story.

00:02:05.740 --> 00:02:07.260
There's been a misunderstanding.

00:02:07.270 --> 00:02:09.970
All right? I'm not a criminal.

00:02:10.060 --> 00:02:12.010
I'm a milkman on a delivery.

00:02:12.070 --> 00:02:14.020
I know you got a beef with the girl.

00:02:14.380 --> 00:02:15.690
That ain't got nothing to do with me,

00:02:15.700 --> 00:02:16.240
right?

00:02:16.840 --> 00:02:19.060
I don't give a f*** about your delivery.

00:02:19.090 --> 00:02:21.820
What I do give a f*** about is how you

00:02:21.820 --> 00:02:23.500
would happen to have this.

00:02:24.460 --> 00:02:27.550
I have spent decades building outposts

00:02:27.550 --> 00:02:30.100
and checkpoints, but this map manages

00:02:30.100 --> 00:02:32.110
to avoid damn near every one.

00:02:32.440 --> 00:02:34.270
I want the name of your cartographer.

00:02:34.300 --> 00:02:36.640
My catero-- to what?

00:02:37.300 --> 00:02:38.590
Your mapmaker.

00:02:38.830 --> 00:02:39.970
Oh, no.

00:02:40.150 --> 00:02:41.980
I found that on the side of the road.

00:02:41.980 --> 00:02:43.000
Dude, come on.

00:02:43.000 --> 00:02:44.290
You want it? Take it.

00:02:44.320 --> 00:02:45.970
You really think I'm that stupid?

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:47.200
No, no, no, no, no, no.

00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:49.210
Not at all. I know how this world

00:02:49.210 --> 00:02:50.530
works, Officer.

00:02:52.480 --> 00:02:54.280
Little respect. I appreciate that.

00:02:54.280 --> 00:02:56.650
But for the record, it's agent.

00:02:56.680 --> 00:02:59.250
Even better. Agent Stone.

00:02:59.260 --> 00:03:01.570
I didn't know this map avoided your

00:03:01.570 --> 00:03:03.640
routes. I did not know.

00:03:03.640 --> 00:03:05.200
Now I do know.

00:03:05.200 --> 00:03:06.940
So how about I get one of those

00:03:06.940 --> 00:03:08.890
licenses I keep hearing so much about

00:03:08.890 --> 00:03:10.540
and I go on my merry way.

00:03:10.840 --> 00:03:13.270
Go. Whoa! Why did you do that?

00:03:19.470 --> 00:03:20.730
Oh, that was unnecessary.

00:03:20.810 --> 00:03:21.120
Oh.

00:03:27.620 --> 00:03:29.240
Couldn't even do it yourself.

00:03:35.070 --> 00:03:36.900
We'll revisit that attitude in a few

00:03:36.900 --> 00:03:37.500
hours.

00:03:38.170 --> 00:03:39.000
I can't wait.

00:03:44.880 --> 00:03:45.310
Get the name of the

00:03:45.550 --> 00:03:47.730
mapmaker.

00:03:47.730 --> 00:03:48.980
One leak could bring the whole dam down.

